# Local dev secrets for `wrangler pages dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored)
# and fill in real values. Do NOT commit `.dev.vars`.
#
# How to obtain each:
#
# WORKOS_CLIENT_ID / WORKOS_API_KEY
#   All sign-in runs through WorkOS AuthKit (/api/auth/workos/*).
#   Create a dev environment at https://dashboard.workos.com → grab the
#   client id ("client_...") and an API key ("sk_..."), and register
#   http://localhost:3002/api/auth/workos/callback as a redirect URI.
#   Use a SEPARATE dev environment from prod — never share credentials.
#
# SESSION_SIGNING_KEY
#   Any 32-byte random string. Reserved for future HMAC of state cookies.
#   `openssl rand -base64 32` works.
#
# ABUSE_NOTIFY_EMAIL
#   In dev anything is fine (e.g. dev@localhost). Production points at
#   abuse@spool.pro and gets the manual D1 polling treatment until v1.1
#   wires Mailchannels.
#
# ADMIN_USER_IDS
#   Comma-separated list of user ids allowed to hit /api/admin/audit.
#   In dev you'll discover your own user id by signing in once and
#   reading the `users` row from the local D1 sqlite file; paste it back
#   here and restart wrangler dev to admin yourself.

# PUBLIC_BASE_URL
#   The origin OAuth start/callback bake into the redirect_uri sent to
#   WorkOS. In dev this MUST be the share-web vite server (the /api/*
#   proxy origin), not wrangler's own :8788 — and it must match the
#   redirect URI registered in the WorkOS dashboard, or every web
#   sign-in fails with a redirect_uri mismatch. Unset in prod (defaults
#   to https://spool.pro).

# DEV_WORKOS_API_URL (optional — normally injected by share-dev.sh)
#   workerd ignores proxy envs (workers-sdk#4515); on proxy-only dev
#   networks point server-side WorkOS calls at the share-web vite relay:
#   http://localhost:3002/__dev/workos. Leave unset otherwise.

WORKOS_CLIENT_ID=
WORKOS_API_KEY=
SESSION_SIGNING_KEY=
ABUSE_NOTIFY_EMAIL=dev@localhost
ADMIN_USER_IDS=
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3002
